# ChatGPT–Cursor handoff

This rule applies to this repository.

## Before continuing phased work

1. Read `docs/CHATGPT_CURSOR_HANDOFF.md`.
2. Treat its frozen evidence, authorization boundaries, Current blockers and
   Next authorized task as binding.
3. Stay on the recorded branch and existing draft PR unless the current task
   explicitly names a different branch and PR.

## Authorization boundaries

- Never overwrite immutable experiment evidence listed in the handoff
  (kernel versions, frozen config/prompt/schema hashes, prior fail records).
- Never run gold studies or execute
  `notebooks/07_kaggle_second_reader_gold_constrained.ipynb` unless the
  current task explicitly authorizes gold (`gold_rerun_authorized=true` in
  that task).
- Never process the 4,349 report-only studies unless the current task
  explicitly authorizes it.
- Never merge the recorded PR or open a replacement PR unless the current
  task explicitly asks for that.
- Never modify recorded scientific results to make a gate pass.

## End of every task

1. Update `docs/CHATGPT_CURSOR_HANDOFF.md` using the Cursor completion
   protocol in that file (UTC timestamp, phase, starting and ending SHAs,
   files changed, commands/tests, sanitized results, unresolved failures,
   gold/report-only access, recommended next decision).
2. Post or update one sanitized summary on the existing PR. Begin new
   handoff comments with `[CHATGPT_HANDOFF_READY]`. Do not spam duplicate
   comments; update the existing handoff comment when one exists.
3. Finish the user-facing response with: repository full name, PR URL,
   branch, HEAD SHA, PR-comment URL, and `CHATGPT_HANDOFF_READY`.

## Privacy

Never put credentials, tokens, cookies, private data, report text,
completions, logits, patient identifiers or competition-record rows in Git
or PR comments. Do not commit `.whl` files, model weights, DICOM, or
private datasets.
